  "notes": "Headline 145 t is \"over front with special equipment\" (** in chart, 13.1 m @2.5 m) - excluded (set null) because it is not a 360° rating. 13.1 m @3.0 m (110.6 t) and @3.5 m (101.5 t) are marked * \"with special equipment\" (kept). Per source note, the table shows the best performance at each boom length among plural telescoping patterns, so values may rise with radius within a column (e.g. 35.0 m 35.2 -> 38.7 t) and no strength/stability line is shown. Capacities are rated lifting capacities; hook block mass (1,080 kg for 100 t, 610 kg for 45 t, 300 kg for 7.2 t) and slings must be deducted (operation note 3). Outrigger longitudinal span = 4,520 + 4,505 mm (outrigger centres to slewing centre, plan view p.1); transverse max 8.2 m (min 2.99 m). Operating weight and max hook height not stated numerically. DIMS (p.1): 3 axles; overall 16,190 = 8,045 (boom head to 1st axle) + 4,000 + 2,000 + 2,145; carrier length 10,155 in drawing (table also lists \"carrier length for traveling approx. 8,260 mm\") -> axles at 2.01/6.01/8.01 m from carrier front; slewing centre 1,100 mm ahead of 2nd axle (4.91 m); boom foot pin 2,400 mm behind slewing centre; tail swing 4,600. Tyre 26.5R25 diameter not printed (null). | 2026-09-24: special-equipment ratings [110.6, 101.5] set to null (conservative)."
